No third-party code

A conformant Bolina node builds from this repository and a standard toolchain
alone, with the network disabled (SPEC.md §11.7, BE-DEP-01). This repository
therefore vendors no third-party source.

One dependency exists and is not in this repository: the four cryptographic
primitives (Ed25519, X25519, ChaCha20-Poly1305, BLAKE2s) come from the Zig
standard library. They are third-party code with an upstream, and the
constant-time assumption rests on them. This is stated plainly in
THREAT-MODEL.md §4.8 and T1 rather than hidden behind the zero-dependency
claim.
